course: dictionary
lesson: 9456
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one fits. Read the words around the word first. «After the final whistle your muscles need repairing and refuelling, so a proper meal or snack with starchy food and some protein, like a sandwich, pasta, yoghurt or a glass of milk, is part of the training.» Food, meal and protein are the clues, so starchy here means containing starch.
explain: Clothes can be starchy too. A starchy collar is stiff because it has been treated with starch, so it stands up and does not bend. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: People can be starchy as well, but this meaning is informal, so it is used in everyday talk. If someone is starchy, they are stiff, formal and unfriendly. Only the context tells you which meaning is right, so always read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Starchy food contains starch, a kind of carbohydrate found in potatoes, bread, rice, pasta and corn.
fact: Starchy food gives the body energy, and wholegrain starchy food is best.
fact: Starchy clothes are stiff because they have been treated with starch.
fact: (Informal) A starchy person is stiff, formal and unfriendly.
fact: In science, iodine turns blue-black when it touches starch.
exercise: «Starchy carbs like bread, pasta, rice and potatoes are the body's main fuel for running about.» What does starchy mean in this sentence? | Made of paper | Stiff and formal | *Containing starch, a kind of carbohydrate | Very hot
exercise: Mum ironed Sam's shirt, and the starchy collar stood up stiffly. What does starchy mean here? | Soft and warm | *Stiff, because it was treated with starch | Wet from the rain
exercise: «The new head teacher was so starchy that nobody dared to smile.» What does starchy mean? | Friendly and funny | *Stiff, formal and unfriendly | Very noisy | Full of starchy food
test: «In the Eatwell Guide about a third of the plate is fruit and veg and just over a third is starchy food.» What is starchy food in this sentence? | *A food group such as pasta, rice, potatoes and bread | Clothes that have been ironed | Food that is only sweet
test: Ella says her uncle is starchy at every family party. What does she mean? | He is loud and funny | He eats only starchy food | *He is stiff, formal and unfriendly
exam: «Starchy food gives the body energy and helps you run about.» Which meaning fits best? | Glowing in the dark | *Containing starch, a kind of carbohydrate | Very old | Stiff and formal
